[I] Lua event loop using coroutines

[T] cqueues is a continuation queue module for Lua, an event loop built on
[T] coroutines and epoll or kqueue. It provides non-blocking sockets with
[T] TLS, DNS resolution, signals, threads and file change notification.

[U] https://25thandclement.com/~william/projects/cqueues.html

[A] Lua-cqueues Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/base
[F] CROSS

[V] 20261006
[L] MIT

[D] bb6e711932854269d8a62bb3cd2eedac4dda72ed84bf554b91a6c832 cqueues-20261006.tar.gz https://github.com/wahern/cqueues/archive/rel-20261006/

. $base/package/*/*/lua-conf.in

luaapi=${luaver/./}
var_append makeopt ' ' "LUA_APIS=$luaver LUA${luaapi}_CPPFLAGS= lua${luaapi}cpath=$pkglibdir lua${luaapi}path=$pkgdatadir"
var_append makeinstopt ' ' "LUA_APIS=$luaver LUA${luaapi}_CPPFLAGS= lua${luaapi}cpath=$pkglibdir lua${luaapi}path=$pkgdatadir"
